{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["The sense of <b>\"And those that came, male and female of all flesh, came\"</b> is that those who came into the ark were male and female, which Noah brought inside it accordingly, and therefore it says, \"as Elohim commanded him,\" for He commanded him to bring them inside it. Now the opinion of Rabbi Abraham is that <b>\"And Noah went in, and his sons, and his wife, and his sons' wives with him, into the ark\"</b> (Genesis 7:7) — they did not enter inside it, but rather they all came to it on the seventeenth day of the second month, for his house was near the ark. And the sense of <b>\"because of the waters of the flood\"</b> is: out of fear of the waters of the flood; and for the seven days the waters of the flood were coming, and they all gathered into the ark, and he closed the entrance and the window. But his words are not correct. Rather, it is possible that <b>\"And Noah did according to all that YHWH commanded him\"</b> and <b>\"And Noah was six hundred years old\"</b> and the verses through <b>\"in the six hundredth year\"</b> (Genesis 7:5–6) are not recounting the event, but rather <b>\"And Noah did according to all that YHWH commanded him\"</b> encompasses the entire matter — it says that he did everything he was commanded; he omitted nothing of the entire matter: he made the ark, gathered the food, and took from the animals and the birds, the clean ones seven pairs each, on the day that He commanded him. And when he was six hundred years old and the flood came upon the earth, he came with his household and with the clean animals and all the living creatures into the ark as Elohim commanded him. And afterwards (from verse 10 onward) Scripture recounts the event: <b>\"And it came to pass after the seven days\"</b>, <b>\"in the six hundredth year\"</b>, and completes the matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The citation \"on the seventeenth day of the second month\" reflects Ibn Ezra's reading of the timeline; the Hebrew literally says בעשור לחדש השני, 'on the tenth of the second month,' which follows Rashi's reading of the chronology in v. 11."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:20:45.492949387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}